---
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { LEGAL } from '../data/legal';

const days = LEGAL.refundWindowDays;
const toc = [
  ['summary', 'In short'],
  ['first-payment', `${days}-day refund`],
  ['not-refundable', 'What isn’t refundable'],
  ['cancel', 'Cancelling'],
  ['balance', 'Balance and add-ons'],
  ['request', 'How to ask'],
  ['law', 'Your legal rights'],
  ['errors', 'Billing errors'],
  ['contact', 'Contact'],
] as const;
---

<Docs
  title="Refund Policy — Truplexy"
  description={`Truplexy refund policy: a ${days}-day refund on your first payment for a paid plan, how cancelling works, and how to ask.`}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Refund Policy', path: '/refunds' }]}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Refund Policy"
  lede={`Try a paid plan with a ${days}-day safety net. Last updated ${LEGAL.updated}.`}
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="summary">In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The first payment for a paid plan (Starter or Pro) is refundable in full within <strong>{days} days</strong> of purchase.</li>
    <li>After that, payments are not refunded, but you can cancel at any time and keep access until the period you paid for ends.</li>
    <li>The {LEGAL.trialDays}-day free trial costs nothing. Cancel before it ends and you are not charged, so there is nothing to refund.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Our orders are processed by {LEGAL.paddle.name}, which is the Merchant of Record. Refunds are paid back through {LEGAL.paddle.name} to the payment method you used.
  </p>

  <h2 id="first-payment">{days}-day refund on your first payment</h2>
  <p>
    If you buy a paid plan and it is not for you, ask for a refund within {days} days of the date of that first payment and
    we will refund it in full, no questions asked. This covers the first payment for your account, whether you chose
    monthly or yearly billing.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The {days} days start on the day the payment is taken. If you started with the free trial, that is the day the trial ends and your payment method is first charged.</li>
    <li>It applies once per customer. If you cancel, get a refund and later buy again, the new purchase is not eligible for the {days}-day refund.</li>
    <li>If you ask in time, a refund of a first payment ends the paid plan. Your account and its data stay, but its assistants stop replying until a new plan starts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="not-refundable">What isn’t refundable</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Renewals.</strong> Automatic renewals of monthly or yearly plans. Cancel before the renewal date if you do not want to be charged.</li>
    <li><strong>Used tokens and usage.</strong> Token add-ons that have been used, and replies already billed against your balance (including overage), because the AI model cost has been incurred.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments after the {days} days</strong> of your first payment, and upgrades after that window, other than as described under <a href="#law">Your legal rights</a> and <a href="#errors">Billing errors</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Accounts closed for breaking our <a href="/terms#acceptable-use">acceptable-use rules</a>.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Third-party costs,</strong> such as fees charged by messaging platforms or other services you connect.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cancel">Cancelling</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel a paid plan at any time. Cancelling stops the next renewal. You keep the plan, and its limits, until the
    end of the period you have already paid for. After that your account and its data stay, but its assistants stop replying until
    a new plan starts. We do not refund the
    unused part of a period after the {days}-day window.
  </p>
  <p>
    Downgrading to a cheaper plan or to a shorter billing period works the same way: it takes effect at the end of the
    paid period. If we end the service altogether, we will refund prepaid fees for the time left, as stated in the <a href="/terms#termination">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="balance">Balance and add-ons</h2>
  <p>
    Funds you add to your account balance pay for token add-ons and for replies after your plan’s monthly tokens run out.
    If you ask within {days} days of adding funds, we will refund the part of that payment you have not used. Used funds
    and add-on tokens already consumed are not refundable. Add-on tokens expire at the end of the month they are bought
    in; unused tokens do not roll over and are not refunded after the {days}-day window.
  </p>

  <h2 id="request">How to ask</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.supportEmail}`}>{LEGAL.supportEmail}</a> from the address on your account, or contact {LEGAL.paddle.name} through the link in your payment receipt, within the {days} days.</li>
    <li>Tell us the business name and, if you have it, the order or invoice number. A reason helps us improve but isn’t required.</li>
    <li>We aim to reply within 3 business days. Approved refunds are issued through {LEGAL.paddle.name} to your original payment method, and your bank may take 5–10 business days to show it. We cannot refund to a different method.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    {LEGAL.paddle.name}’s <a href={LEGAL.paddle.help} rel="noopener noreferrer">help centre</a> explains its side of
    payments. Its <a href={LEGAL.paddle.terms} rel="noopener noreferrer">buyer terms</a> apply to the purchase too.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">Your legal rights</h2>
  <p>
    This policy doesn’t take away rights you have under the law where you live, such as a statutory cooling-off period or a
    remedy for a service that wasn’t as described. Where such a right applies, it applies in addition to this policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="errors">Billing errors</h2>
  <p>
    If you were charged the wrong amount, charged twice, or charged after a cancellation that went through in time, tell us
    and we will fix it and refund the difference, whenever it is spotted. Report it as soon as you can; the sooner, the
    easier it is to trace.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.supportEmail}`}>{LEGAL.supportEmail}</a><br />
    <a href={LEGAL.entityUrl}>{LEGAL.entity}</a>, {LEGAL.address}
  </p>
  <p>
    See also: <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>
  </p>
</Docs>
